  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 210 PM MST MON NOV 16 2026\nA closed upper low continues to impact the area Thursday through \nFriday. Continuous valley rain and mountain snow is expected, \nbeginning to taper off Friday. 0.20 inches of rain will fall by \nearly Friday. Latest long-range guidance has snow levels hanging in \nthe 3500-4500 ft range through Saturday. Valleys may see a rain/snow \nmix Friday morning, before precipitation completely tapers off by \nlate Friday/early Saturday. Most central ID mountains are forecast \nto receiver around 1-2 inches of snow, up to 3-7 inches in the S-\nCentral ID mountains, and around 3-7 inches again in Eastern OR \nmountains. By early Saturday, the system will steer out of our area \nand a ridge develops overhead. This brief dry period will be \nlimited, as long-term guidance has another Pacific upper trough \nmoving into the northwest and into the eastern OR side by late \nSaturday. Slight chances of valley rain or rain/snow mix and \nmountain snow showers are forecast for late Saturday through early \nMonday, with higher terrain areas seeing the bulk of total precip \nand snow.",
